    {
      "id": "hld-corners-text",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 150,
      "y": 4900,
      "width": 1455,
      "height": 1000,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "aaN",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1060,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 2060,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1786350000000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "fontSize": 23,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "text": "CORNER CASES / WHAT IF?\n\nEMPTY SELECTION\nCommands keep their existing single-object behavior.\n\nONE SELECTED OBJECT\nThe selected set is still authoritative; Copy and Delete must not use a stale activated object.\n\nLOCKED, PINNED, GROUND-TRUTH, OR UNSUPPORTED TARGET\nValidate before mutation. Disable or reject the complete operation and explain the incompatible target.\nShift+Delete is the explicit exception that force-deletes locked objects.\n\nFRAME CHANGE OR ANNOTATION REFRESH\nClear selection on frame changes. Reconcile client IDs after same-frame refreshes; remove stale IDs.\n\nHIDDEN OR NO-LONGER-RENDERED OBJECT\nDo not begin a visual group move when every selected target cannot participate consistently.\n\nMASK, SKELETON, TRACK, AND MIXED SHAPE TYPES\nUse operation-specific capability rules. Do not silently move only a supported subset.\n\nCOPY THEN SOURCE CHANGES OR IS DELETED\nClipboard data must be serialized snapshots, not live ObjectState references.\n\nPASTE ON ANOTHER FRAME OR LAYER\nUse the destination frame and current layer while preserving geometry relative to the copied group.\n\nSHORTCUT COLLISION\nSelection starts only with the configured modifier by itself; Ctrl+Shift+Z must remain Redo.\n\nBACKEND OR CORE FAILURE AFTER COMMAND STARTS\nRoll back the complete batch, keep history consistent, refresh annotations, and preserve an actionable error.",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "CORNER CASES / WHAT IF?\n\nEMPTY SELECTION\nCommands keep their existing single-object behavior.\n\nONE SELECTED OBJECT\nThe selected set is still authoritative; Copy and Delete must not use a stale activated object.\n\nLOCKED, PINNED, GROUND-TRUTH, OR UNSUPPORTED TARGET\nValidate before mutation. Disable or reject the complete operation and explain the incompatible target.\nShift+Delete is the explicit exception that force-deletes locked objects.\n\nFRAME CHANGE OR ANNOTATION REFRESH\nClear selection on frame changes. Reconcile client IDs after same-frame refreshes; remove stale IDs.\n\nHIDDEN OR NO-LONGER-RENDERED OBJECT\nDo not begin a visual group move when every selected target cannot participate consistently.\n\nMASK, SKELETON, TRACK, AND MIXED SHAPE TYPES\nUse operation-specific capability rules. Do not silently move only a supported subset.\n\nCOPY THEN SOURCE CHANGES OR IS DELETED\nClipboard data must be serialized snapshots, not live ObjectState references.\n\nPASTE ON ANOTHER FRAME OR LAYER\nUse the destination frame and current layer while preserving geometry relative to the copied group.\n\nSHORTCUT COLLISION\nSelection starts only with the configured modifier by itself; Ctrl+Shift+Z must remain Redo.\n\nBACKEND OR CORE FAILURE AFTER COMMAND STARTS\nRoll back the complete batch, keep history consistent, refresh annotations, and preserve an actionable error.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.2
    },
    {
